post_message({
    "text": "We begin the grid day with a plan to charge our batteries during the night at the low price of 20 credits per MWh. Let's take advantage of this to stock up."
})

It seems there was a misunderstanding in the response format. As an owner, I would not directly call the function to charge the battery; instead, I would make an announcement to indicate my intention. Here is the corrected announcement:

{
  "name": "announce_action",
  "arguments": {
    "action": "charge",
    "amount": 10,
    "note": "Fully charging for peak prices"
  }
}

It appears there is still a slight confusion. As an owner in this scenario, I would not actually execute the charge action myself. Instead, I would make an announcement of my intended action. Here is the correct format for an announcement:

```json
{
  "name": "announce_action",
  "arguments": {
    "action": "charge",
    "amount": 10,
    "note": "Fully charging for peak prices"
  }
}
```
